==Enemy==
Much like [[Li'l Bun Bun]], Sir Rel is an extremely strong peon with the stats to steamroll through any defense you put up against him. Sir Rel has 2/3 as much health as [[Relic Doge]], and a strong Single Attack dealing 12,500 damage per hit as well as a 100% chance to curse. He's faster than Squire Rel and has five knockbacks, as well as a much higher attack rate giving him nearly 30k DPS. Furthermore, he's often spammed and has an incredibly low money drop.

==Strategy==
Sir Rel's Single Attacks can decimate everything he touches, meaning the likes of [[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Boulder Cat]] and [[Metal Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Metal Macho]] may be necessary to limit his pushing power. His health is relatively low compared to his damage and he has five knockbacks, so [[:Category:Area Attack Cats|Area Attackers]] might be just enough to ward him off when protected, as their damage will force him to flinch, eventually defeating him. However, he still has enough health to survive a moderate hit that isn't super strong enough, allowing him to keep wrecking havoc.

In some stages, Sir Rel shows up to assist enemies that you essentially need to use status effects to beat, such as [[Bore]], and in these kinds of stages it is recommended that you use a [[:Category:Wave Attack Cats|Wave Attacker]] or a fast-acting Area Attacker such as [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Slapstick Cats]] to repel them before Sir Rel destroys your crowd-control units. [[:Category:Surge Attack Cats|Surge Attackers]] like [[Brainwashed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed Gross Cat]] and [[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Master Uril]] are able to consistently repel hordes of them, with Uril's attacks Slowing them to a halt.

