==Trivia==
*Sir Rel's Japanese name, イングリッス ''Ingurissu'', is a pun on イングリッシュ ''Ingurisshu'' (English) and 栗鼠 ''risu'' (squirrel).
*His Japanese description implies that he learned English from [[Squire Rel]] via time travel, but since Squire Rel couldn't articulate, he isn't any better.
*The time machine in Sir Rel's Japanese description may explain how he appears in [[Cats of the Cosmos]] Chapter 3's [[Zombie Outbreaks]].
*Since [[Revival of Origin]] features a [[Media:Bg1028.gif|huge, glowing tree]], the stage's Squire Rel or Sir Rel may represent [[wikipedia:Ratatoskr|Ratatoskr]], a squirrel in Norse mythology who runs up and down the world tree [[wikipedia:Yggdrasil|Yggdrasil]] to carry messages between the eagle perched atop the tree and [[wikipedia:Nidhogg|Nidhogg]], the serpent below the tree.
*He may have been inspired by the 40,000% Squire Rels from [[Apple Bobbing Ocean]], which have 18,000 less HP, but deal only 500 less damage per hit than a 100% Sir Rel (12,500 > 12,000).
*Despite being introduced after [[Oldhorn]], Sir Rel is listed before him in the [[Enemy Guide]] and has a lower ID.
*Sir Rel and [[Relic Doge]] are the only [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relic enemies]] to appear in the [[Main Chapters Levels|Main Chapters]], both in Cats of the Cosmos Chapter 3's Zombie Outbreaks.
*Sir Rel and [[Haniwanwan]] are the only Relic enemies to have [[Single Attack]].
*He has the lowest health and money drop of all Relic enemies.

